# QA & Test Strategy

## 1. Quality Objectives

- What "quality" means for this product specifically
- Quality priorities (rank order): correctness > performance > security > UX > ...
- Acceptable defect rates by severity at launch
- Quality gates that must pass before each release

## 2. Test Pyramid

### Layer 1: Unit Tests
- **Coverage target**: X% line coverage, Y% branch coverage
- **What to unit test**:
  - Business logic and domain rules
  - Data validation and transformation
  - Utility functions and helpers
  - State machines and status transitions
- **What NOT to unit test**:
  - Framework boilerplate
  - Simple CRUD without logic
  - Third-party library internals
- **Tools**: [specific test framework, mocking library]
- **Run cadence**: Every commit, in CI pipeline

### Layer 2: Integration Tests
- **Coverage target**: All service boundaries and data flows
- **What to integration test**:
  - Database operations (repository layer)
  - API endpoint request/response cycles
  - Message queue producers and consumers
  - External service integrations (with contract stubs)
  - Authentication and authorization flows
- **Test database strategy**: Separate test database, migrations applied per run, data cleanup between tests
- **Tools**: [specific tools]
- **Run cadence**: Every PR, in CI pipeline

### Layer 3: Contract Tests
- **What to contract test**:
  - API contracts between frontend and backend
  - Event schema contracts between producers and consumers
  - Integration contracts with external systems
- **Tools**: Pact / Spring Cloud Contract / custom schema validation
- **Run cadence**: Every PR, blocking merge

### Layer 4: End-to-End Tests
- **Coverage target**: Critical user journeys only (not comprehensive E2E)
- **What to E2E test**:
  - Core user journeys (list specific journeys from user stories)
  - Payment flows (if applicable)
  - Onboarding flow
  - Authentication flows
- **Tools**: [Playwright / Cypress / Selenium]
- **Environment**: Staging environment with test data
- **Run cadence**: Before release, nightly on staging

### Layer 5: Manual / Exploratory Testing
- **When**: Before major releases, after significant changes
- **Focus**: Edge cases, UX quality, cross-browser/device, accessibility
- **Who**: QA team + product team

## 3. Functional Test Scope

### Critical Business Flows

For each critical user journey identified in the user stories:

| Journey | Test Type | Automated? | Priority | Test Cases | Owner |
|---------|----------|-----------|----------|-----------|-------|
| User registration & onboarding | E2E + Integration | Yes | P0 | 8-12 | QA |
| Core value delivery flow | E2E + Integration | Yes | P0 | 15-20 | QA |
| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |

### Business Rule Testing

| Rule ID | Test Approach | Test Cases | Happy Path | Edge Cases | Negative Cases |
|---------|-------------|-----------|-----------|-----------|---------------|
| BLR-001 | Unit test | 5 | 1 | 2 | 2 |
| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |

### Error & Edge Case Coverage

For each critical flow, explicitly test:
- Invalid input combinations
- Concurrent access scenarios
- Partial failure and recovery
- Timeout and retry behavior
- Permission boundary violations
- Rate limiting enforcement
- Data at boundary values (min, max, empty, null)

## 4. Non-Functional Testing

### Performance Testing
- **Tool**: k6 / Locust / Artillery / JMeter
- **Test types**:
  - Load test: Sustained expected load for 30 minutes
  - Stress test: 2x-5x expected load to find breaking point
  - Soak test: Expected load for 4+ hours to find memory leaks
  - Spike test: Sudden traffic surge

**Performance Test Scenarios**:

| Scenario | Endpoint/Flow | Target | Concurrent Users | Duration | Pass Criteria |
|----------|-------------|--------|-----------------|----------|--------------|
| API read latency | GET /api/v1/[resource] | p95 < 200ms | 500 | 30 min | p95 < 200ms, error rate < 0.1% |
| API write throughput | POST /api/v1/[resource] | > 100 rps | 200 | 30 min | Throughput > 100 rps, p99 < 1s |
| Core journey | End-to-end flow | < 3s total | 100 | 30 min | Completion < 3s, 0 errors |
| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |

### Security Testing
- **OWASP Top 10 assessment**: Automated scanning + manual review
- **Authentication testing**: Token expiry, session management, brute force protection
- **Authorization testing**: Privilege escalation, IDOR, horizontal access
- **Input validation**: SQL injection, XSS, CSRF, command injection
- **Dependency scanning**: Known CVEs in dependencies
- **Secrets scanning**: No secrets in code, configs, or logs
- **Tools**: OWASP ZAP / Burp Suite / Snyk / Trivy
- **Run cadence**: Dependency scan every commit, full scan before release

### Accessibility Testing
- **Standard**: WCAG 2.1 Level AA
- **Automated**: Axe / Lighthouse accessibility audit — zero critical/serious violations
- **Manual**: Screen reader testing (VoiceOver, NVDA), keyboard navigation
- **Color contrast**: Minimum 4.5:1 ratio for text
- **Test cadence**: Every major UI change

### Compatibility Testing
- **Browsers**: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge (latest 2 versions)
- **Mobile**: iOS Safari, Android Chrome
- **Screen sizes**: 320px - 2560px
- **Test approach**: Automated visual regression + manual spot checks

## 5. Test Data Management

### Test Data Strategy
- **Approach**: Factory-based test data generation / Fixtures / Anonymized production data
- **PII handling**: No real PII in test environments
- **Data setup**: Before each test run / Shared baseline dataset
- **Data cleanup**: After each test run / Nightly cleanup

### Test Data Sets

| Dataset | Purpose | Size | Refresh Cadence | Contains PII? |
|---------|---------|------|----------------|--------------|
| Seed data | Baseline for all tests | Small | Per migration | No |
| Load test data | Performance testing | Large (10K+ records) | Before load tests | No (synthetic) |
| Edge case data | Boundary and error testing | Small | As needed | No |

## 6. Test Environments

| Environment | Purpose | Data | Deploy Frequency | Access |
|------------|---------|------|-----------------|--------|
| Local | Developer testing | Local DB, mocked externals | Continuous | Developers |
| CI | Automated tests | Ephemeral DB, mocked externals | Every commit/PR | CI system |
| Staging | Integration + E2E | Realistic data, real integrations (sandbox) | Every merge to main | Team |
| UAT | User acceptance | Curated test scenarios | Before release | Product + QA |

## 7. User Acceptance Testing (UAT)

### UAT Plan
- **Who**: Product owner, key stakeholders, beta users
- **When**: End of each sprint for sprint-level UAT, formal UAT before release
- **Duration**: 3-5 business days for release UAT

### UAT Scenarios

| Scenario | Persona | Steps | Expected Outcome | Tested By |
|----------|---------|-------|-----------------|----------|
| ... | ... | Step-by-step | ... | Role |

### UAT Exit Criteria
- All P0 scenarios pass
- No critical or high-severity defects open
- Product owner sign-off
- Performance SLAs met in staging

## 8. Regression Strategy

- **Automated regression suite**: All P0 + P1 E2E tests
- **Run cadence**: Before every release, nightly on staging
- **Suite maintenance**: Review and prune quarterly
- **Flaky test policy**: Quarantine after 3 flakes, fix within 1 sprint or delete

## 9. Defect Management

### Severity Definitions

| Severity | Definition | Response SLA | Fix SLA | Example |
|----------|-----------|-------------|---------|---------|
| Critical (S1) | System down, data loss, security breach | 15 min | 4 hours | Production outage, auth bypass |
| High (S2) | Major feature broken, no workaround | 1 hour | 24 hours | Payment processing failure |
| Medium (S3) | Feature degraded, workaround exists | 4 hours | Next sprint | Slow search, UI glitch |
| Low (S4) | Cosmetic, minor inconvenience | Next triage | Backlog | Typo, alignment issue |

### Defect Lifecycle
- Found → Triaged → Assigned → In Progress → Fixed → Verified → Closed
- Reopen criteria
- Escalation path for disputed severity

## 10. Release Quality Gates

### Pre-Release Checklist

| Gate | Criteria | Owner | Blocking? |
|------|---------|-------|----------|
| Unit tests | 100% pass, coverage >= target | Engineering | Yes |
| Integration tests | 100% pass | Engineering | Yes |
| E2E tests | All P0 pass | QA | Yes |
| Security scan | No critical/high CVEs | Security | Yes |
| Performance | SLAs met in staging | QA | Yes |
| Accessibility | 0 critical violations | QA | Yes (for UI changes) |
| UAT | Sign-off received | Product | Yes |
| Documentation | API docs updated | Engineering | No |

### Definition of Done (per story)
- Code reviewed and approved
- Unit + integration tests written and passing
- Acceptance criteria verified
- No regression in existing tests
- Documentation updated (if API change)
- Accessibility checked (if UI change)

### Definition of Ready (per story)
- Acceptance criteria are testable
- Dependencies identified and available
- Test data requirements documented
- Edge cases identified

